From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:32:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] clk: samsung: Add Tensor G4 core clock paths

Describe TOP shared PLL rate paths, HSI2 storage and PCIe branch clocks,
and the PERIC0 supply-GPIO path using the existing Samsung CMU helpers.
Retain firmware PLL rates, mux selections and dividers; no PLL rate
table is supplied. Only the listed branch gates enter CCF control.

Register fields come from Google's cmucal-sfr.c; ordered parent lists
come from cmucal-node.c. G4 uses the cal-if/zuma implementation as well.
The same OSCCLK_CMU feeds TOP PLLs and oscillator mux entries, so use
one oscclk reference instead of unverified 26 MHz CMU clock aliases.

The original private implementation reached guarded UFS root on the
Pixel 9a, but this revised oscillator description has not been tested
on the phone. No board nodes or complete power management are added.
The shared helper switches listed gates to manual mode, preserving
the current CG bit; board integration must audit handoff gate states.

Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/google-modules/soc/gs/+/204078758737776959ecc85c527a00fd2cabb62f/drivers/soc/google/cal-if/zuma/cmucal-sfr.c
Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/google-modules/soc/gs/+/204078758737776959ecc85c527a00fd2cabb62f/drivers/soc/google/cal-if/zuma/cmucal-node.c
Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/google-modules/soc/gs/+/204078758737776959ecc85c527a00fd2cabb62f/drivers/clk/gs/clk-zuma.c#77
Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
